{# ============================================================ HERO
   Two columns: copy left, photo right — plain, no border/radius/shadow on
   the photo, just the image sitting in its column. #}
<section class="story-hero bg-paper">
  <div class="shell"><div class="page-canvas story-hero-grid">
    <div class="story-hero-copy">
      <span class="eyebrow" data-hero-in>Our Story</span>
      <h1 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-display-2 text-ink text-balance" data-hero-in>
        A journey of <em class="italic text-navy font-book">purpose.</em><br>
        A future of <em class="italic text-gold-text font-book">impact.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-body-lg text-ink-muted max-w-measure-tight leading-relaxed" data-hero-in>
        Since 2015, Admizz Group has worked at the intersection of education and opportunity &mdash; helping students and professionals find the preparation, guidance and pathways to their next milestone.
      </p>
      <a href="#journey" class="story-hero-cta" data-hero-in>
        Our journey
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 3v9M4 8l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="story-hero-photo" data-hero-in>
      {% imageEager "src/assets/images/story/hero-building-branded.png", "The Admizz mark on a building facade, directional brand imagery", "(min-width: 1000px) 44vw, 92vw" %}
    </div>
  </div></div>

  {# Proof block (2026-09-08 v3) — v2 was four equal cards with the numbers
     at display scale, and the client's read was right: "3" and "9" rendered
     fist-sized are underwhelming, not impressive, and four identical boxes
     isn't a composition. Rebuilt around the strongest REAL asset this
     project has — 103 actual partner university marks harvested from
     admizzeducation.com — which had never appeared on this page at all.

     Attribution matters here: universities.json is source:admizzeducation,
     status:draft — Admizz's own published partner list, not independently
     audited — so the caption says so, exactly as the homepage does. The
     ICEF card beside it is the opposite kind of claim: independently
     verifiable, with the real verify route attached. Keeping them adjacent
     but distinct is the honest presentation. #}
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="page-canvas">
      <div class="bento mt-14 md:mt-20">

        <div class="bento-item bento-wide fade-up" style="grid-row: span 1;">
          <div>
            <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">The network</span>
            <p class="mt-3 font-display font-light text-h2 text-ink text-balance max-w-[20ch]">
              <span class="tabular-nums">{{ universities.totalCount }}</span> partner institutions across
              <span class="tabular-nums">{{ destinations.countries | length }}</span> countries.
            </p>
          </div>

          {# Two marks per country group, across the first five groups — a
             representative spread rather than a hand-picked "best" set,
             and it stays correct if the harvested data changes. #}
          <div class="logo-wall">
            {% for g in universities.groups | head(5) %}
              {% for uni in g.universities | head(2) %}
              <span class="logo-tile" title="{{ uni.name }}">
                <img src="{{ uni.logo }}" alt="{{ uni.name }}" width="120" height="72" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
              </span>
              {% endfor %}
            {% endfor %}
          </div>

          <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-3">
            <a href="/ventures/#record-education" class="text-small font-medium text-ink link-underline">See the full network &rarr;</a>
            <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">Published by Admizz Education, as of 2026</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bento-item bento-item-navy fade-up" style="animation-delay:90ms">
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-accent">Accreditation</span>
          <div>
            <p class="bento-num bento-num-word font-display font-light text-navy-on">ICEF</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-small text-navy-on-muted">
              Agency <span class="tabular-nums">IAS&nbsp;6499</span>, held by Admizz Education &mdash; verifiable at ICEF directly, not self-reported.
            </p>
            <a href="https://www.icef.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-small font-medium text-navy-on link-underline">
              Verify with ICEF
              <svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10L10 4M10 4H5.5M10 4v4.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bento-item bento-item-tint fade-up" style="animation-delay:170ms">
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-text">Operating since</span>
          <div>
            <p class="bento-num font-display font-light tabular-nums text-ink">{{ site.founded }}</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-small text-ink-muted">Founded in Denver, Colorado &mdash; still the group&rsquo;s headquarters, now behind three businesses.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ THE JOURNEY
   2026-09-08 v3: was a vertical dotted timeline — text left, small photo
   far right, a scrubbed connector line down the side. Two problems, both
   measured rather than assumed: rows sprawled with ~500px of dead paper
   between the copy and its photo, and the whole track sat left-aligned
   inside the 95vw shell, leaving 820px of empty page down the right at a
   1890px window (what the client circled).

   Rebuilt as alternating claim + visual rows, the device the SaleUnion
   reference uses for its own numbered sections: mono year label, a large
   display heading, the copy, and a substantial image plate opposite —
   sides swapping each row so the page has rhythm instead of one long
   left-hugging column. Content is capped and centred (.page-canvas), so
   both margins match at any width.

   The dotted-line/dot markup and its GSAP scrub are gone with it; the
   arrival animation is the same index-staggered .fade-up used elsewhere,
   so nothing here depends on JS to become visible. #}
<section id="journey" class="story-journey-section bg-paper-sunk py-section border-t border-rule" data-stack-outgoing>
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="page-canvas">
      <span class="eyebrow fade-up">The Journey</span>
      <h2 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-h1 text-ink max-w-[18ch] text-balance fade-up" style="animation-delay:80ms">
        Milestones that shaped who we are.
      </h2>

      <div class="mt-12 md:mt-16">
        {% for t in timeline %}
        <article class="journey-row">
          <div class="journey-copy fade-up" style="animation-delay:{{ loop.index0 * 60 }}ms">
            <p class="journey-year font-display font-light tabular-nums">{{ t.year }}</p>
            <h3 class="mt-4 font-display font-book text-h2 text-ink text-balance max-w-[16ch]">{{ t.label }}</h3>
            <p class="mt-4 text-body-lg text-ink leading-relaxed max-w-measure-tight">{{ t.text }}</p>
            {# timeline.json has carried an `impact` sentence per milestone
               since the file was written and no template ever rendered it —
               every entry showed only the one-line `text`, which is why
               this section read as thin. Existing content, now shown. #}
            {% if t.impact %}
            <p class="mt-5 pt-5 border-t border-rule text-body text-ink-muted leading-relaxed max-w-measure-tight">{{ t.impact }}</p>
            {% endif %}
          </div>

          {# Plate: a photo where a meaningful one exists, a DESIGNED DATA
             PANEL where it doesn't. timeline-2020.jpg was a stock sunset
             sky and timeline-today.jpg an abstract glass facade — neither
             said anything about its milestone, and no real Admizz
             photography exists for them. Rather than swap in more
             meaningless stock, those two rows now carry the actual data
             the milestone is about (the real destination list; the real
             venture list), which is also the device the reference uses:
             its right-hand panels are designed information, not photos.
             Replace with real photography if the client supplies it —
             the photo branch below already handles it. #}
          {% if t.year == "2020" %}
          <div class="data-panel data-panel-navy fade-up" style="animation-delay:{{ loop.index0 * 60 + 90 }}ms">
            <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-accent">Where we place students</span>
            {# Anchors the panel's top — without it the label floated alone
               above a large void, since the list is bottom-aligned. #}
            <p class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-navy-on">
              <span class="bento-num tabular-nums">{{ destinations.countries | length }}</span>
              <span class="ml-2 text-h4 text-navy-on-muted">study destinations</span>
            </p>
            <div class="data-panel-grid">
              {% for c in destinations.countries %}
              <span class="data-panel-row">
                <span aria-hidden="true">{{ c.flag }}</span>
                <span class="text-small text-navy-on">{{ c.name }}</span>
              </span>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
          </div>

          {% elif t.year == "Today" %}
          <div class="data-panel fade-up" style="animation-delay:{{ loop.index0 * 60 + 90 }}ms">
            <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">The group today</span>
            <p class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-ink">
              <span class="bento-num tabular-nums">{{ ventures | length }}</span>
              <span class="ml-2 text-h4 text-ink-muted">connected businesses</span>
            </p>
            <div class="data-panel-list">
              {% for v in ventures %}
              <span class="data-panel-item">
                <span class="font-mono text-small tabular-nums text-navy-soft">{{ v.index }}</span>
                <span>
                  <span class="block font-display font-book text-h4 text-ink">{{ v.name }}</span>
                  <span class="block mt-0.5 font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">{{ v.vertical }}</span>
                </span>
              </span>
              {% endfor %}
            </div>
          </div>

          {% else %}
          <div class="journey-plate fade-up" style="animation-delay:{{ loop.index0 * 60 + 90 }}ms">
            <span class="journey-plate-badge bento-tag" aria-hidden="true">{{ "0" }}{{ loop.index }} / {{ t.year }}</span>
            {% image "src/assets/images/story/" + t.image, t.imageAlt, "(min-width: 900px) 38vw, 92vw" %}
          </div>
          {% endif %}
        </article>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ THREE BUSINESSES
   Same subjects as /ventures/, a lighter-touch summary here with a direct
   link to each record. "Learn more" points at the real in-page anchor
   /ventures/ already exposes (verified: id="record-{id}" on that page). #}
<section class="story-businesses-section bg-paper py-section" data-stack-incoming>
  <div class="shell"><div class="page-canvas">
    <span class="eyebrow fade-up">Our Businesses</span>
    <h2 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-h1 text-ink max-w-[18ch] text-balance fade-up" style="animation-delay:80ms">
      Three businesses. <em class="italic text-navy font-book">One purpose.</em>
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-ink-muted max-w-measure-tight leading-relaxed fade-up" style="animation-delay:120ms">
      Different focus areas, a shared conviction that access to opportunity shouldn&rsquo;t depend on where someone starts.
    </p>

    {# 2026-09-06: ascending-tone staggered treatment (reference: Scalient's
       3-step process cards, light-to-accent intensity) — was a flat,
       identical 3-column grid (the same "sameness" pattern already flagged
       and fixed elsewhere on the site, e.g. Beliefs). Card 1 stays the
       plain paper-raised tier; card 2 steps up to a stronger border/shadow;
       card 3 (Work — the group's newest, most active-growth venture) is
       the boldest, inverted to navy. A real index numeral (v.index, already
       in ventures.json) is added per card — nothing new invented, and it's
       the same numbering device used on /ventures/. #}
    <div class="story-venture-grid mt-10">
      {% for v in ventures %}
      <article class="story-venture-card story-venture-card-{{ loop.index }}" data-story-venture-card>
        <span class="story-venture-num" aria-hidden="true">{{ v.index }}</span>
        <span class="story-venture-icon story-venture-icon-{{ v.id }}" aria-hidden="true">
          {% if v.id == "institute" %}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" focusable="false"><path d="M3 17l1-4 9-9 3 3-9 9-4 1z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
          {% elif v.id == "education" %}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" focusable="false"><circle cx="10" cy="10" r="7.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/><path d="M2.5 10h15M10 2.5c4 4.5 4 10.5 0 15-4-4.5-4-10.5 0-15z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4"/></svg>
          {% else %}
          <svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" focusable="false"><path d="M3 16V9M8 16V4M13 16v-5M18 16V7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
          {% endif %}
        </span>
        <h3 class="mt-4 font-display font-book text-h4">{{ v.name }}</h3>
        <p class="story-venture-vertical mt-1 font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest">{{ v.vertical }}</p>
        <p class="story-venture-text mt-3 text-small leading-relaxed">{{ v.verticalLine }}</p>
        <a href="/ventures/#record-{{ v.id }}" class="story-venture-link">
          Learn more
          <svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10L10 4M10 4H5.5M10 4v4.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </a>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ STATEMENT
   2026-09-08: the page ran paper → grey → paper → grey → CTA with no
   tonal peak anywhere, so the story had no moment that landed. This is
   the same navy statement device the homepage already uses, reusing the
   exact .statement-line hook (main.js staggers those phrase-by-phrase on
   scroll, generic and page-agnostic) rather than inventing a second
   motion idiom. Copy is written framing, not a new factual claim — it
   restates the "three businesses, one group" positioning already
   established on /ventures/ and in the section directly below. #}
<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-navy-deep py-section-sm">
  {% include "partials/grain-texture.njk" %}
  <div class="shell relative"><div class="page-canvas">
    <p class="font-display font-light text-h1 text-navy-on max-w-[38ch] text-balance">
      <span class="statement-line inline-block">Preparation, education and work</span>
      <span class="statement-line inline-block italic text-navy-accent font-book">aren&rsquo;t three industries.</span>
      <span class="statement-line inline-block">They&rsquo;re three stages of the same</span>
      <span class="statement-line inline-block">decision &mdash; so we built for all three.</span>
    </p>
    <span class="statement-line inline-block mt-8 md:block font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-on-muted">&mdash; Why the group exists</span>
  </div></div>
</section>

{# ============================================================ LEADERSHIP #}
{# 2026-09-08: was `shell grid [22rem_1fr] items-start` on the full
   min(95vw,2200px) shell — the 1fr text column absorbed the entire
   remaining width while the statement inside stayed at its own measure,
   so the block dead-ended in ~200px of empty grey before the CTA. The
   row now has a reading-width cap of its own and centres its two
   columns against each other, same fix applied to the timeline track
   above. Portrait gets the rounded plate treatment the rest of the site
   uses for photography (.venture-plate, insights cards) instead of a
   bare square of navy. #}
<section class="bg-paper-sunk py-section border-t border-rule">
  <div class="shell">
   <div class="page-canvas grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,19rem)_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-10 md:gap-14 items-center">
    <div class="fade-up">
      <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-navy-deep aspect-[4/5] [&_picture]:block [&_picture]:h-full [&_img]:block [&_img]:h-full [&_img]:w-full [&_img]:object-cover [&_img]:object-top">
        {% image "src/assets/images/people/founder.png", "Manish K Sah, Founder & CEO of Admizz Group", "(min-width: 768px) 19rem, 90vw", [400, 640, 900] %}
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fade-up" style="animation-delay:100ms">
      <span class="eyebrow">Leadership</span>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display font-light text-h2 text-ink max-w-[16ch] text-balance">A vision for what&rsquo;s next.</h2>
      {# Not a blockquote: no verified personal quote from the founder exists
         in the audit (docs/01-AUDIT.md) for admizz.com itself -- the previous
         version presented invented, paraphrased marketing copy in quotation
         marks as if he'd said it. Replaced with a plain, factual statement
         (site.founder.statement) grounded only in facts already established
         elsewhere on the site. A real quote is an open content request. #}
      <p class="mt-8 font-display italic font-book text-h3 text-ink leading-snug max-w-measure text-balance">
        {{ site.founder.statement }}
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-body font-medium text-ink">{{ site.founder.name }}</p>
      <p class="text-small text-ink-muted">{{ site.founder.title }}, {{ site.founder.org }}</p>
    </div>
   </div>
  </div>
</section>

